  "has_quantitative_results": true,
  "summary": "The paper implements two quantum generative models for financial data using a Qiskit Aer simulator: a qGAN with a 15‑qubit variational generator trained for 2000 epochs on ~5000 Binance cryptocurrency samples (batch size 1000) and a 5‑layer QCBM trained to reproduce the same distribution using optimizers such as COBYLA and SPSA. Results show expected GAN loss convergence (~0.693 equilibrium) and qualitative distribution matching, but all experiments are simulator-based with no quantitative classical baseline comparison.",
